                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game seems like a joke at first but it is actually one of the most comprehensive Open World Survival RPGs\n\nhobo tough life For me ranks on a survival difficulty settings similar to Games like The Long Dark BUT It is also an RPG The game plays much more like a classic RPG where you level up your character and gain new better items \n\nIf you love survival games and you love RPGS you will love this game \n\nThe problems I have with this game are few and easy to rectify (Even though I think this game will be getting updates anytime soon)\n\nLoading screens are extremely annoying You could be walking into an area and not even realizing it's a loading screen until you've already hit it And these loading screens can be upwards of ten minutes If the game prompted you to go to a loading screen before entering a door this would be very easy thing to fix (The problem is usually on the other side of the loading screen there isn't even anything there They have like a room with a few things you can steal but it's not worth sitting through a 10 minute loading screen) or if they just removed it from the game entirely\n\nDespite some of the characters having Some level of relatability most characters just kind of seem Very one sided Even though their dialog suggests they are often more complicated I would personally just try to do less telling and more showing on the Characters\n\nOverall this is actually one of the best survival RPGS out there Highly highly recommend if you like survival and RPGS\n9/10",
